'''Shin-ichiro Miki''' (Japanese: '''三木眞一郎''' ''Miki Shin'ichirō'') is a Japanese voice actor for {{aniseries|PTS}}.

==Biography==
Miki was born on March 18, 1968, in {{wp|Tokyo}}, {{wp|Japan}}, and he became a voice actor as an adult. He was both one of the original and one of the longest-serving voice actors in {{aniseries|PTS}}, with his most famous role being [[James]]. He is also noted for voicing most depictions of {{p|Charizard}} and {{p|Golbat}} in various [[Pokémon]] media (including ''Pokémon the Series'' itself), which are left undubbed in many foreign versions of the franchise, including English. Miki is currently affiliated with the talent agency {{wp|81 Produce}}.

